# M2-708: three false positives, and a different class from everything above.
#
# Not a planted secret. `generic-api-key` matched the literal text
# `reserved_at=OCCURRED` -- a keyword-argument name and a module-level test constant --
# because `idempotency_key=` appears earlier on the same line and puts the rule's
# keyword within range. Entropy 3.784, which clears the default threshold.
#
# The trigger is line *shape*, not content, and it was reproduced with gitleaks 8.30.1:
# the rule fires only when the line ENDS immediately after `reserved_at=OCCURRED`. The
# same arguments on a line with a trailing `)`, or split one-per-line with a trailing
# comma, do not match -- which is why only 3 of the 26 `idempotency_key=key` call sites
# in this branch were flagged. They were the three that ruff had wrapped that way.
#
# The three sites have since been split one-argument-per-line, matching the other 23 and
# the surrounding style, so no new commit carries the shape. That does not retire these
# entries and cannot: the commits below stay reachable forever, exactly as the M1-301
# lesson above records. Suppressing by commit-pinned fingerprint keeps the narrowness --
# a real secret at any other line, file or commit still fails the gate.

